# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# WHY eol=lf and not bare text=auto: `text=auto` alone still hands Windows a CRLF
# working tree under core.autocrlf=true, and this repo is compared byte-for-byte
# against a second clone (the canonical skills marketplace). On 2026-08-15 that
# cost a real false alarm — 33 of 53 skills reported as drifted with zero content
# differences. Pinning the working tree to LF makes every clone byte-identical, so
# a cross-clone compare means what it says. See CLAUDE.md § Sitecore skills.
#
# .githooks/* and *.sh are executed by sh: a CRLF shebang line breaks them outright.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary — never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary

